      <h2>Gold Mining Equipment for Ghana</h2>
      <p>Ghana is West Africa's leading gold producer and one of the largest in the world. Active alluvial mining stretches from the Ashanti Region through the Western and Eastern Regions, fed by the Pra, Birim, Ankobra, and Tano rivers. Our wash plants are container-ready for Ghanaian ports and engineered for the heavy clay, laterite, and tropical conditions miners face on the ground.</p>
      <h3>Why Ghanaian Miners Choose Us</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Container-ready for shipping into Tema and Takoradi</li>
        <li>Mercury-free operation — meets Ghana Minerals Commission requirements</li>
        <li>Handles laterite, ironstone, and heavy clay deposits typical of the Ashanti belt</li>
        <li>Simple operation — minimal training required for local crews</li>
        <li>Built for tropical heat, high humidity, and rainy-season conditions</li>
        <li>30-minute setup means more productive hours per day</li>
